dsv41 patch 0085b (24.10.2026): give the allocator's unused cache back after long prefills, only while the engine is idle.
Why: on GB10 GPU memory is system RAM. With PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True, torch.accelerator.empty_cache()
can unmap the physical pages of unused cached segments, but the engine never asks, so after the longest prefill so far
the transient memory stays reserved (measured +1.7–2.0 GiB MemAvailable after a release).
How: the worker counts prefill tokens; when the engine core is about to block on an empty input queue with nothing in
flight, at least one step ran, and no request arrives within VLLM_DSV41_RELEASE_GRACE_S (5 s), it calls
collective_rpc("dsv41_release_if_due"); each rank then synchronizes and empties its cache once if the threshold was
reached. The worker method never raises (a failure reply would desynchronize collective_rpc).
Switches: VLLM_DSV41_RELEASE_TOKENS (threshold, 0 = off), VLLM_DSV41_RELEASE_FILE (file with the threshold, read at
every idle check, overrides it live; set the same on all nodes). Neither set = original behaviour.
